---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Excerpt from "../../components/Excerpt.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import Rule from "../../components/Rule.astro";
import Sequence from "../../components/Sequence.astro";
import { firstPartyPlugins } from "../../lib/manifests.ts";

const P = "cli/src/iki_cli/plugin.py";
const B = "cli/src/iki_cli/deploy.py";
const D = "server/src/iki_server/plugins/deploy.py";
const firstParty = firstPartyPlugins();
const H = {
  short: "A lockfile in, an image out, one transaction on deploy",
  how: "Pinning, building and deploying",
  example: "One plugin in two lockfiles",
  rules: "What a build produces, and what a deploy refuses",
  ref: "Commands and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "lockfile", label: "The lockfile" },
  { id: "build", label: "The build" },
  { id: "deploy", label: "A deploy, step by step" },
  { id: "example", label: H.example },
  { id: "rules", label: H.rules },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      A deployment's config repository holds a lockfile that pins each plugin to a commit. <code
        >iki deploy build</code
      > fetches those commits, checks every plugin together, and writes a Django app for each into
      the deployment's own image, on top of Iki's. When the cluster applies the new image, the
      chart's migrate Job runs Iki's migrations, then every plugin's migrations, the database
      guards they need and the app role's grants in one transaction, before any new pod starts.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Each deployment pins its plugins and builds its own image (<Adr n="0034" />).</li>
      <li>Configuration is GitOps, one repository per deployment (<Adr n="0015" />).</li>
      <li>A deploy's migrations and their guards commit together or not at all (<Adr n="0134" />).</li>
    </ul>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <h3 id="lockfile">The lockfile</h3>
    <p>
      <code>plugins.lock.yaml</code> lists each plugin with a git URL, a path and a full commit, a
      state (<code>active</code>, <code>detached</code> or <code>purged</code>) and, optionally, a
      settings file (<Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/lockfile.py" sym="def load_lock(" />). A <code
        >local</code
      > entry, a directory instead of a commit, is for development: the build needs <code
        >--allow-local</code
      > and the server refuses it unless told otherwise. Iki's own plugins may come from a mirror of
      Iki's repository, accepted only at a tree Iki's repository has had (<Adr n="0114" />).
    </p>
    <h3 id="build">The build</h3>
    <p>
      <code>iki deploy build</code> reads the lockfile and fetches only the pinned commits. Then it
      checks that nothing still active needs a plugin being purged, validates all plugins together,
      refuses an active plugin that depends on a detached one, checks the deployment's settings and
      compute, writes the apps, and fails if any plugin's migrations don't match its manifests (<Path
        p={B}
        sym="def run_build("
      />). It also bundles each plugin's code for workers. <Path p="deploy/plugins.Dockerfile" />{" "}
      copies the apps onto Iki's server image, owned by root and read-only to the server.{" "}
      <code>iki plugin build</code> does the same for one plugin in its own repository (<Path
        p={P}
        sym="def run_build("
      />).
    </p>

    <h3 id="deploy">A deploy, step by step</h3>
    <p>What happens between a merged lockfile change and new pods serving it.</p>
    <Sequence
      id="deploy-seq"
      title="A deploy of a plugin change"
      width={900}
      actors={[
        { id: "repo", label: "Config repo", sub: "CI" },
        { id: "build", label: "iki deploy build" },
        { id: "cluster", label: "Cluster", sub: "GitOps applies" },
        { id: "job", label: "Migrate Job" },
        { id: "db", label: "Postgres" },
      ]}
      steps={[
        { id: "pr", from: "repo", to: "build", label: "every PR: build and check the pinned plugins" },
        { id: "image", from: "repo", to: "repo", label: "on merge: verify Iki's signatures, build, sign, pin by digest" },
        { id: "apply", from: "repo", to: "cluster", label: "image.yaml updated; Argo CD or Flux applies the chart" },
        { id: "job", from: "cluster", to: "job", label: "the migrate Job runs before new pods" },
        { phase: "migrate_deployment" },
        { id: "refuse", from: "job", to: "job", label: "refuse: newer Iki, missing plugin, changed migration…" },
        { id: "own", from: "job", to: "db", label: "Iki's own migrations, each in its transaction" },
        { id: "one", from: "job", to: "db", label: "one transaction: purges, plugins' migrations, sync, grants" },
        { id: "pods", from: "cluster", to: "cluster", label: "new pods; a too-powerful role never turns ready" },
      ]}
    >
      <div slot="pr"><p>Fetches each plugin at its commit, and fails on mismatched migrations, a missing dependency, or an active plugin that depends on a detached one.</p><p><Path p={B} sym="def _detached_alone(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="image"><p>Builds the server image and the worker image, after verifying Iki's images with cosign; signs both; then opens a pull request pointing <code>image.yaml</code> at them by digest (<Adr n="0017" />).</p><p><Path p="deploy/config-template/.github/workflows/build.yml" />, <Path p="deploy/config-template/plugins.Dockerfile" /></p></div>
      <div slot="apply"><p>Merging that pull request deploys; reverting it rolls back. Data moves between deployments only in bundles (<Adr n="0015" />).</p><p><Path p="deploy/config-template/README.md" /></p></div>
      <div slot="job"><p>The Job runs as the migrator role, the only one that owns tables (<Adr n="0025" />).</p><p><Path p="deploy/helm/iki/templates/migrate-job.yaml" /></p></div>
      <div slot="refuse"><p>Also refused: a non-atomic plugin migration, and blocking preflight findings not acknowledged in the chart's <code>acknowledgePreflight</code> (<Adr n="0181" />).</p><p><Path p={D} sym="def _check_preflight(" />, <Path p="deploy/helm/iki/values.yaml" sym="acknowledgePreflight" /></p></div>
      <div slot="own"><p>Some of Iki's own migrations build indexes <code>CONCURRENTLY</code>, which can't run inside a transaction. None of them touches a plugin's table.</p></div>
      <div slot="one"><p>So a deploy's migrations and the guards that hold its records are applied or rolled back together: other connections see the old schema with its guards until the commit, then the new one with its guards (<Adr n="0134" />).</p><p><Path p={D} sym="def _unguard(" />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/core/management/commands/grant_app_privileges.py" /></p></div>
      <div slot="pods"><p>Readiness checks the app role's privileges (<Adr n="0025" />).</p><p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/health.py" />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/core/db_roles.py" /></p></div>
    </Sequence>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={3} title={H.example}>
    <p>
      On the dev cluster, <Path p="plugins/lots" label="iki/lots" /> is a local directory, so editing
      it rebuilds the cluster's image:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file="deploy/dev/plugins.lock.yaml" start="^  - \{ name: iki/lots" />
    <p>A real deployment pins a commit, as the config template's staging lockfile does:</p>
    <Excerpt file="deploy/config-template/deployments/staging/plugins.lock.yaml" start="^  - name: iki/dna" />
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title={H.rules}>
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="What a build produces" open>
        <p>
          One package per plugin, <code>iki_plugin_&lt;namespace&gt;__&lt;name&gt;</code>: <code
            >apps.py</code
          >, <code>models.py</code>, <code>manifest.json</code> with the hosts its actions name
          through settings filled in, <code>settings.json</code> for a deployment, the plugin's own
          migrations copied unchanged, and its components checked against their digests. Beside
          them, <code>iki_installed_plugins</code> lists the apps in dependency order with the Iki
          version that built them and, for a deployment, where each plugin came from. The same
          inputs always give the same bytes (<Path p="codegen/src/iki_codegen/build.py" />).
        </p>
        <p>
          The core plugin is built the same way by <code>make core</code> into <Path
            p="server/src/iki_plugin_iki__core"
          />, and a test fails while that app is behind its manifests (<Path
            p="scripts/build_core.py"
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Fetching plugins">
        <p>
          Only https and ssh URLs, never prompting, never a URL with credentials in it; no hooks,
          submodules or LFS; every object checked, and the fetched commit checked to be the one
          asked for. A plugin is exported from the commit, never run from a working copy. An{" "}
          <code>iki/*</code> plugin from a mirror is accepted only at a tree listed in <Path
            p="spec/src/iki_spec/first_party_trees.json"
          />, and git config that redirects Iki's repository is refused (<Path
            p="cli/src/iki_cli/fetch.py"
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="What the migrate Job refuses" id="refusals">
        <p>
          A database a newer Iki migrated; a plugin missing from the build unless the lockfile purges
          it; a migration that changed after it was applied; a plugin migration that isn't atomic;
          and blocking preflight findings nobody acknowledged. Rolling back means deploying an older
          lockfile: the Job reverses the migrations the build lacks only if no reversal can lose
          data, and otherwise changes nothing and says why (<Path p={D} sym="def migrate_deployment(" />,{" "}
          <Adr n="0034" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="sync_plugins" id="sync">
        <p>
          In the same transaction, it puts back what the database enforces for the installed
          plugins: HRID sequences, never dropped; comments on every table and column; the read-only{" "}
          <code>iki_views</code> views; triggers for unique fields, reference edges, rules, the types
          a reference may name, and locked records; and an analyst role if one is named (<Path
            p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/sync.py"
            sym="def sync("
          />, <Adr n={[120, 127]} />). What those triggers hold: <PageLink to="States and guards" />,{" "}
          <PageLink to="Saving and validation" />.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="First-party plugins and their trees">
        <p>
          Iki's {firstParty.length} plugins live in <Path p="plugins" /> with their own versions, and
          must validate with their dependencies, have matching migrations, build, migrate forwards
          and back, and store entities (<Adr n="0039" />, <Path
            p="server/tests/test_first_party_plugins.py"
          />). <code>make first-party</code> adds each
          plugin's current git tree to the trees file, and a test fails while one is missing (<Path
            p="scripts/first_party_trees.py"
            sym="def tree("
          />). The list and what each does: <PageLink to="All plugins" />. Who owns lots,
          inventory, samples, requests, lab roles and instruments is set by <Adr n="0211" />.
        </p>
        <p>
          First-party images are built and signed like Iki's own, from <code
            >plugins/&lt;plugin&gt;/images/</code
          > (<Adr n="0065" />, <Path p="plugins/protein/images" />). Wasm modules some actions call
          are checked before they reach a worker: <PageLink to="WebAssembly" />.
        </p>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <div class="refs">
      <div>
        <h3>Commands</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><code>iki plugin build</code> <Path p={P} sym="def run_build(" label="plugin.py" /></li>
          <li><code>iki deploy build</code> <Path p={B} sym="def run_build(" label="deploy.py" /></li>
          <li><code>iki-server migrate_deployment</code> <Path p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/management/commands/migrate_deployment.py" label="command" /></li>
          <li><code>iki-server sync_plugins</code> <Path p="server/src/iki_server/core/management/commands/sync_plugins.py" label="command" /></li>
          <li><code>make core</code>, <code>make first-party</code> <Path p="Makefile" /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Decisions</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><Adr n="0015" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0034" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0039" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0114" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0134" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0211" title /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
